[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm very new to LEAN and have a lot of experience with Rocq and Iris in Rocq. What is the solution to the problem of needing to write <code>iprop(..)</code> everywhere? <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Binding.20arguments.20to.20.22notation.20scopes.22/near/611262291\">#general &gt; Binding arguments to \"notation scopes\" @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 611271906,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784289504
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>iprop(...)</code> is roughly the same as the <code>%I</code> notation scope in Rocq--sometimes you need it to disambiguate, other times you don't. We also added a notation <code>iprop%</code> which will swallow the rest of the line inside an <code>iprop(...)</code> and can save some parens.</p>",
        "id": 611273681,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784290018
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But there isn't an easy way to bind this to types <code>Bind Scope</code> or argument positions <code>Arguments .. _%foo</code> in LEAN?</p>",
        "id": 611275774,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784290665
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In Lean, the best we could hope for is the following</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iprop</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ptsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ptsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ignore</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ptsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ignore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cond</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">els</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">els</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, with how <code>iprop%</code> (or <code>iprop(...)</code>) is currently implemented, it doesn't propagate down <code>match</code> nor function calls. I see no reason why it couldn't, though</p>\n<p>However, yeah, there's no way to bind a scope to a type in Lean, which is why the original <code>iprop%</code> is inevitable</p>",
        "id": 611276094,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784290777
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Gemini seems to suggest that to simulate this, people wrap macros around functions</p>",
        "id": 611276416,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784290861
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>that seems pretty heavy-handed</p>",
        "id": 611276642,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784290937
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, that's what we do with entailment, for instance, which introduces the <code>iprop</code> annotations directly. But since you're building the <code>PROP</code> directly, we can't really avoid the <code>iprop</code>.</p>",
        "id": 611276695,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784290957
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We could make a <code>funI x =&gt; </code> notation that would implicit wrap the body in <code>iprop</code></p>",
        "id": 611276843,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291002
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Btw, this is not only a limitation that we've run into. The <code>Std.Do</code> framework has a similar definition for their <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/51b8e4a6e9d542e705c0e1d8e7a171603fc1b255/src/Std/Do/SPred/Notation.lean\"><code>SPred</code></a>. I mention this because, if they find a better way of doing it, we could copy it and viceversa</p>",
        "id": 611276868,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291009
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"955633\">Gregory Malecha</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/The.20need.20for.20prop/near/611276843\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We could make a <code>funI x =&gt; </code> notation that would implicit wrap the body in <code>iprop</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The issue is that, after every <code>match</code>, you'd need to introduce it again. This helps to hide the first <code>iprop</code>, but so far the consensus has been that having an <code>iprop%</code> at the beginning of your definition is unobstrusive enough</p>",
        "id": 611277093,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291074
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>and if i wanted to write something like monadic bind, e.g. <code>letI* x := e in k</code>, then I could probably add the <code>prop</code> within that notation definition.</p>",
        "id": 611277372,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291154
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Seconding Fernando. I found that with <code>iprop%</code> it's a little annoying but not really that bad in practice. We actually considered <code>letI</code>, but it's a little ad-hoc and sort of tricky to generalize to all binding forms. You can always add this notation locally though!</p>",
        "id": 611277630,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784291233
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, it's always fine to define extra notations for these kinds of usecases. Just let me point out that <code>let</code> already propagates <code>iprop</code>, if I remember correctly, so you shoudln't need to define a  custom notation for it.</p>",
        "id": 611277709,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Let me also reference a longer discussion about this in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Why.20is.20.60iprop.28.2E.2E.2E.29.60.20needed.3F\">#iris-lean &gt; Why is &#96;iprop(...)&#96; needed?</a></p>",
        "id": 611277784,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291283
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah, what i want is <code>letI*</code> to be a monadic bind operator in the <code>iprop</code> monad</p>",
        "id": 611277915,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291326
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this lets you write things like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ret</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611278035,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291361
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here, <code>v1</code> and <code>v2</code> are resources?</p>",
        "id": 611278155,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291390
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>no, they are values</p>",
        "id": 611278215,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291398
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>wp : Expr -&gt; (Nat -&gt; PROP) -&gt; PROP</code></p>",
        "id": 611278262,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291412
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>so this is basically the CPS monad</p>",
        "id": 611278310,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291425
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, I didn't understand that to be <code>iprop</code></p>",
        "id": 611278356,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291435
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In any case, I think it'd be nice to have an issue asking for <code>iprop(..)</code> to propagate over <code>match</code> statements</p>",
        "id": 611278464,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291462
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this was mentioned somewhere in the conversation I linked to previously, but idk if we opened an issue for it. Feel free to open an issue if you'd like, or I can open it later myself if you'd prefer</p>",
        "id": 611278562,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784291503
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder if the \"interpretation scope\" setup of Rocq would be a useful thing for LEAN to have in general.</p>",
        "id": 611278566,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1784291505
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"690100\">Fernando LEAL</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/The.20need.20for.20prop/near/611278464\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In any case, I think it'd be nice to have an issue asking for <code>iprop(..)</code> to propagate over <code>match</code> statements</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If you have some clear examples of what kind of usages you'd want to work, I'd be happy to have a look at implementing this; I should have some time over the weekend.</p>",
        "id": 611285198,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Keizer",
        "timestamp": 1784293419
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think just making this snippet work would aready be great (see <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Binding.20arguments.20to.20.22notation.20scopes.22/near/611262291\">#general &gt; Binding arguments to \"notation scopes\" @ 💬</a>  for the missing definitions)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iprop</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ptsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ptsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ignore</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ptsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">addr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ignore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cond</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">els</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">els</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'm thinking of some rule for <code>match</code>, which I believe you worked on before (I thought it was merged?), and then one for function application, either <code> `(iprop($f $xs*)) =&gt; `($f $(←xs.mapM (fun x =&gt; `(iprop($x)))))</code> or maybe something more fancy where you only put it around the arguments of type <code>PROP</code> by inspecting <code>f</code> first. Idk if more complexity would be worth it though</p>",
        "id": 611286279,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784293758
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(deleted)</p>",
        "id": 611286830,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1784293930
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I prototyped some things, but IIRC didn't polish and submit a PR before, mostly cause I wasn't sure how much complexity was justified.</p>",
        "id": 611290413,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Keizer",
        "timestamp": 1784294983
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"690100\">Fernando LEAL</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/The.20need.20for.20prop/near/611286279\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[...] or maybe something more fancy where you only put it around the arguments of type <code>PROP</code> by inspecting <code>f</code> first. Idk if more complexity would be worth it though</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>At first glance, that feels like it might be a bit too magical. I think I'd start with wrapping all arguments first, and then let's see if that's good enough. Is there an established way of embedding a regular term inside <code>iprop(...)</code> already? Then we could just rely on users un-embedding if they need regular arguments to their function?</p>",
        "id": 611291489,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Keizer",
        "timestamp": 1784295276
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"481133\">Alex Keizer</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/The.20need.20for.20prop/near/611291489\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is there an established way of embedding a regular term inside <code>iprop(...)</code> already? </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I believe there's a <code>term(..)</code> analog, although I haven't actually seen it used</p>",
        "id": 611303797,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784298636
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's the first PR, for <code>iprop(match ...)</code>: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/525\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/525</a></p>",
        "id": 611550069,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Keizer",
        "timestamp": 1784489251
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"690100\">Fernando LEAL</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/The.20need.20for.20prop/near/611276868\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Btw, this is not only a limitation that we've run into. The <code>Std.Do</code> framework has a similar definition for their <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/51b8e4a6e9d542e705c0e1d8e7a171603fc1b255/src/Std/Do/SPred/Notation.lean\"><code>SPred</code></a>. I mention this because, if they find a better way of doing it, we could copy it and viceversa</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Do note though that I copied the notation last year from the initial one in <code>iris-lean</code> that has been there since Lars König's Master's thesis :) I just took an existing approach and did not evaluate whether it could be made better. Your <code>iprop%</code> indeed sounds like it's better.</p>\n<p>A macro wrapping <code>iprop%</code> around a term is indeed IMO the logical extension of the idea... for example, you could define a <code>idef%</code> command that expands to <code>def</code>+<code>iprop%</code>, or the proposed <code>funI</code> that expands to <code>fun</code>+<code>iprop%</code>. You simply need <em>some</em> way to teach the parser that you expect an <code>iprop</code> at some position rather than a plain <code>term</code>; it can't be purely expected-type-driven like it appears to be in Rocq.</p>",
        "id": 611811680,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1784612931
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130195\">Sebastian Graf</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/The.20need.20for.20prop/near/611811680\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I just took an existing approach and did not evaluate whether it could be made better. Your <code>iprop%</code> indeed sounds like it's better.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I see, I had been hoping that you decision meant that this was the best we could do for now. It's still true that any improvements made in one project could be adapted by the other and viceversa, but maybe now it's worth looking at it more throughouly</p>",
        "id": 611835854,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1784622924
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW, I plan to retire the entire SPred machinery soon. The only remaining syntax will be that for embedding pure Props. I will move the old proof mode into a <a href=\"https://github.com/sgraf812/lattice-proof-mode\">lattice proof mode package</a> with much weaker maintenance guarantees.</p>",
        "id": 611849574,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1784627305
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another ... interesting clash with Std.Do is the current notation for embedding pure propositions. I'm just playing around with a separation logic and noticed that the current lattice-based definition <code>def ofProp p := if p then \\top else \\bottom</code> is not the right notion for separation logics, where you also want to intersect with <code>emp</code> (the empty heap assertion).</p>\n<p>No conclusion here yet, but it would be great if we could arrive at a coherent notion of \"embedding a pure proposition\". it is a shame that <code>emp</code> is necessary just because it is the neutral element of sep conjunction... Maybe you have an idea to resolve this?</p>",
        "id": 613601805,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1785402628
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I talked with Sebastian U and he suggested that another potential solution would be to use a coercion to interpret the notation</p>",
        "id": 613622795,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1785410462
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not knowing lean, I would guess this is some variation on</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- st `i &lt; j`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasForall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">forall</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prop</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But marked as a coercion that is always inlined.</p>",
        "id": 613623114,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1785410605
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130195\">Sebastian Graf</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/The.20need.20for.20prop/near/613601805\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm just playing around with a separation logic and noticed that the current lattice-based definition <code>def ofProp p := if p then \\top else \\bottom</code> is not the right notion for separation logics, where you also want to intersect with <code>emp</code> (the empty heap assertion).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>In Iris, <code>⌜P⌝</code> does not include <code>emp</code>, but is equivalent to your <code>ofProp</code>:  </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Decidable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊣⊢@</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">PROP</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">by_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(Though in practice you often want to use <code>⌜P⌝ ∧ emp</code>.)</p>",
        "id": 613640419,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1785416424
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>BlueRock used <code>only_provable</code> with <code>[| P |]</code> and it was <strong>very</strong> useful.</p>",
        "id": 613662397,
        "sender_full_name": "Gregory Malecha",
        "timestamp": 1785422209
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>In Iris, <code>⌜P⌝</code> does not include <code>emp</code>, but is equivalent to your <code>ofProp</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Ah, that's great to know, thanks. (Unrelatedly, we should clean up Init so that PartialOrder.rel is actually LE.le; it's on my radar but not scheduled yet.)</p>",
        "id": 613672758,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1785424667
    }
]